A minor version that breaks compatibility with its predecessor. The authoring
form derives major vs. minor from this check, so a compiler won't produce this,
but BindLineage still checks it.

The error carries no position at all. BindLineage positions it at the schema
value's Source(), which is nil for a value with more than one conjunct (thema's
schema!: _ and the author's), so it falls back to a plain error. The compat
checker's detail, in the text only, points at thema's lineage.cue (_schema),
not at either schema.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
}
-- ship/0.1.thema --
schema: {
	title: int
}

backward: {
	title: "untitled"
}
-- out/error --
schema 0.1 is not backwards compatible with schema 0.0:
field title not present in {title:string}:
    /github.com/sdboyer/thema/lineage.cue:227:11
missing field "title"
-- out/positions --
schema 0.1 is not backwards compatible with schema 0.0:
	no positions
